{:edb/db-before-t 321 :edb/db-after-t 322 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533634 50 #inst "2026-10-04T03:46:18.094Z" 13194139533634 true] [17592186147560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243014 13194139533634 true] [17592186147561 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243028 13194139533634 true] [17592186147565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186243021 13194139533634 true] [17592186147896 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533634 true] [17592186147896 1145 "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 4+4\\times 6 \\\\  & =8+24 \\\\  & =32\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186147917 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533634 true] [17592186147917 1145 "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/09eff98ca31b4bb350e2d793dcfa6e6972de25bb3b613c898533068c36fe9a78.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $2\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=2\\times 2=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $2\\,\\text{m}$ and the height is $9\\,\\text{m}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 2\\times 9=9\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =4+4\\times 9 \\\\  & =4+36 \\\\  & =40\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243015 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1089 "q-119208" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/4f2807a0989a3f36376d1ed93d02162ded72200803d28b49caab701176837628.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular pyramid represented by the net above?" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1113 #uuid "8020cab4-3d7d-5a11-9426-5c8de74166ce" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1138 false 13194139533634 true] [17592186243014 1145 "The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 36+4\\times 30 \\\\  & =36+120 \\\\  & =156\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243016 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243017 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243018 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243019 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243020 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1041 "selection" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243019 13194139533634 true] [17592186243015 1110 #uuid "567812c0-b06b-53d3-a732-67726c6b5fb7" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243016 1034 "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533634 true] [17592186243016 1111 #uuid "3e07cb84-d0b4-5170-bb6d-8e0aff34a673" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243017 1034 "144\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533634 true] [17592186243017 1111 #uuid "3bb38e1a-94a3-5217-aca2-aab60076c4b5" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243018 1034 "164\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533634 true] [17592186243018 1111 #uuid "58ef7413-d232-53e3-b05b-cc4e25c64794" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243019 1034 "156\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533634 true] [17592186243019 1111 #uuid "858d11dc-8943-5927-9a54-8f1821d56261" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243020 1034 "148\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533634 true] [17592186243020 1111 #uuid "cd2f358e-d060-5361-9e36-0857128bf9e8" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243022 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1089 "q-62248" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/c241f6afc3978dfc8d1e2a048509a2e6fc7c91b0caf5ac4814a864edc3992d0c.png)\n\nChloe wants to paint a steel box that has the form of a rectangular prism. Two of the polygonal faces are $4\\,\\text{ft}\\times 4\\,\\text{ft}$ squares. If the cost to paint the surface is $$6.50$ per square foot, how much will it cost her in total? Note that Chloe does *not* need to paint the square sides." 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1113 #uuid "abe6fddf-a313-54f2-92c6-9b51675460f7" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1138 false 13194139533634 true] [17592186243021 1145 "The net of our prism is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/7b84a48933abb96f605476c6d703406227b0fe5301b1457a447cdbb3f58f0937.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nEach side face (apart from the square faces) of our solid is a rectangle, where the base is $7\\,\\text{ft}$ and the height is $4\\,\\text{ft}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=7\\times 4=28\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, the total area of the side surfaces consists of $4$ rectangular faces. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area of the sides} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle}) \\\\  & =4\\times 28 \\\\  & =112\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the cost to paint the surface is $$6.50$ per square foot, the total amount that Chloe will have to pay is\n\n$$\n112\\times 6.50=$728.\n$$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243023 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243024 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243025 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243026 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243027 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1041 "selection" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243023 13194139533634 true] [17592186243022 1110 #uuid "75904f92-8b53-52a8-9ce0-04342c711241" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243023 1034 "$$728$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533634 true] [17592186243023 1111 #uuid "8eed53d2-4cb0-5293-b007-12540aad1a3c" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243024 1034 "$$211$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533634 true] [17592186243024 1111 #uuid "d941a6d5-c450-5474-a23a-d9d374030b08" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243025 1034 "$$782$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533634 true] [17592186243025 1111 #uuid "feec887f-d0eb-56d9-8906-0efc8097c725" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243026 1034 "$$827$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533634 true] [17592186243026 1111 #uuid "225e1086-5a1b-5246-ac5e-a62929728648" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243027 1034 "$$112$" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533634 true] [17592186243027 1111 #uuid "2dc158a0-96ab-512d-847b-7ca73f08ca86" 13194139533634 true] [17592186243028 1017 #